# /etc/postfix/header_checks (SSLE): quarantine spam instead of delivering it.
# The spamassassin pipe re-injects every message with X-Spam-Flag: YES when the score is >= 5.0;
# Postfix cleanup then moves it to the hold queue. Postfix logs "hold: header X-Spam-Flag: YES",
# which Wazuh rule 100223 turns into an alert.
#   list quarantined mail : postqueue -j | grep '"queue_name": "hold"'   (or mailq)
#   release one           : postsuper -H <queue id>
#   delete one            : postsuper -d <queue id> hold
/^X-Spam-Flag:[[:space:]]*YES/    HOLD quarantined by SpamAssassin
